C1-Slim device-side source licensing

Unless a file or component contains a different license notice, the
first-party source code in C1ancher/, C1ancher-server/, App/, Pinao/, ChiChuGames/, examples/,
and the repository's documentation and packaging scripts is distributed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0-only).

The complete GPL version 3 license text is included in C1ancher/LICENSE.
This follows the existing core project's GPL v3 license.

Third-party code and assets retain their original licenses; see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the notices in the component directories.

The imported term-ime/ component retains its upstream MIT license declaration
and the individual licenses of its vendored dependencies and data. It is not
relicensed under the repository's GPL default; see term-ime/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The simulator/ component declares GPL-3.0-or-later for its first-party code;
its Linux device module declares GPL-2.0-only. See simulator/LICENSE and
simulator/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for its component-specific notices.

The separately distributed c1publish executables have their own distribution
notices. See the publisher kit's DISTRIBUTION-NOTE.txt and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.
